   111	**Freeze:** both the small-step relation and Q9.9's total fuel-indexed evaluator over instrumented hybrid Core state: `eval(target, layout, environmentChoices, fuel, coreProgram, state)`. This is the reference evaluator for qualification; it executes Core, not BIR or source text. Choices explicitly cover external responses, allocation/address choices, exposed-pointer alternatives and padding materialization. A choice input can be an oracle rather than a finite stream; each answer is checked against the operation contract. Oracle queries are pure deterministic functions of the Core execution history, request kind, logical site and occurrence number, independent of fuel budget; answers are deterministic functions of those queries and the fixed oracle. Materialization queries occur only at C4’s first raw exposure, not on safe borrowing or typed rewrites. Fixed inputs make evaluation deterministic. Native backends need not issue the same queries; P4 checks allowed Core observations instead. Prove evaluator soundness (a reported result has a matching finite execution), completeness (every finite execution is obtained with enough fuel), monotonicity (extra fuel preserves a completed result) and trace-prefix consistency. For nondeterministic effects these statements quantify over the same environment choices.
